    "images": [],
    "plugin": {
      "description": "Adds a customisable radial wheel to Final Fantasy XIV. Assign emotes or macros to slots, organise them across multiple pages, bind a key to open the wheel, and execute them with a single click. Supports per-character and per-page colour theming.\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/AlessHub/DalamudPlugins/main/repo.json",
      "images": [],
      "nsfw": false,
      "official": false,
      "richCard": false,
      "richnessScore": 1302,
      "summary": "A radial wheel for quickly using actions in FFXIV.",
      "webEnriched": true
    },
    "projectRepository": "https://github.com/AlessHub/ActionWheel",
    "schema": "omega.evidence.presentation.v1",
    "website": {
      "description": "A Dalamud plugin for Final Fantasy XIV that adds a customisable radial action wheel.",
      "homepage": "",
      "images": [],
      "links": [
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "label": "Source",
          "url": "https://github.com/AlessHub/ActionWheel"
        }
      ],
      "omegaBannerUrl": "",
      "readmeExcerpt": "# Action Wheel\n\nA [Dalamud](https://github.com/goatcorp/Dalamud) plugin for Final Fantasy XIV that adds a customisable radial action wheel.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Radial wheel UI** — hold your keybind to open the wheel, hover a segment and release to execute the emote\n- **Multiple pages** — organise actions across pages with optional custom names\n- **Per-slot assignment** — assign any unlocked emote or macro to any wheel slot\n- **Chat log option** — toggle whether each emote is sent to the chat log\n- **Per-page colour theming** — override wheel colour, hover colour, and text colour per page\n- **Modifier key support** — optionally require a modifier (Ctrl / Alt / Shift) alongside the main keybind\n\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open the config window via `/actionwheel` or the Dalamud plugin list\n2. Set a **Toggle Key** (the key you hold to open the wheel)\n3. Add emote pages and assign emotes to slots\n4. In game, hold the toggle key — the wheel appears. Hover a segment and release to use that emote\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nThis plugin has been made with AI, vibe-coding, copilot, however you want to name it. I have written some of the code but mostly it's AI written.\nI have however led all of the decisions and read everything personally, made logs to check outputs and outcomes and overall \"built\" the plugin. I understand what it does and how it does it.\n\n\n## License\n\n[GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later](LICENSE)",
      "title": "ActionWheel",
      "url": "https://github.com/AlessHub/ActionWheel"
    }
  },
